{"panneau":"edition-2026-11-07","panneauNom":"Édition du samedi 7 novembre 2026","passages":[{"id":232,"page":"edition-2026-11-07.html","ancre":"edition-2026-11-07","titre":"Édition du samedi 7 novembre 2026","panneau":"Édition du samedi 7 novembre 2026","texte":"φ Le cerveau du site The Site's Brain FR EN L'édition du jour Édition du samedi 7 novembre 2026 Quatrième édition. Le 7 novembre 2026 a été le jour des grandes vagues : six versions du site (52 à 57), le mémoire des propositions de loi publié dans la bibliothèque du site, et la lecture intégrale des fils de discussion Gemini du compte de l'auteur — questions posées et hachages recalculés à l'appui. Les faits ci-dessous sont portés vérifiés [V] au niveau des jalons publics du site et du dossier. Édition nº 4 Le site, le 7 novembre 2026 Signée SoPHIa Sur le site aujourd'hui 7 novembre 2026 — versions 52 à 57 publiées Six versions en un jour Vérifié [V] Le journal du site consigne les six versions du jour : le Miroir complet et les textes aux places stratégiques (52) ; le Miroir à deux modes et les deux volets tranchés (53) ; l'audit du servi devenu la construction (54) ; la base stable — ancres honorées, cerveau rafraîchi, listes canoniques (55) ; la base stable démontrée au servi (56) ; et les finitions de l'audit tour 4 (57). Chaque version publiée est auditée au servi avant que la suivante parte. Ce que ça change pour toi : la boucle construire, publier, vérifier, réparer ne s'arrête pas : ce que l'audit trouve devient la liste de construction de la version suivante. Source : site public — Journal des mises à jour , versions 52 à 57. 7 novembre 2026 — mémoire publié au site Quinze propositions de loi, sept constats Vérifié [V] Le mémoire « Propositions de loi » est publié dans la bibliothèque des lois du site : quinze propositions et sept constats, chacun avec sa justification sourcée. Parmi elles : le droit de contester une déduction qu'une plateforme détient sur toi (la montrer, la contester, la faire corriger), et la ristourne vérifiable sur l'argent fait avec les données des gens. Ce que ça change pour toi : les déductions des plateformes ne sont plus présentées comme sans recours : le mémoire nomme le droit de les voir, de les contester et de les faire corriger — avec une pièce, pas une opinion. Source : site public — Bibliothèque des lois, panneau « Tes données ». 7 novembre 2026 — lecture du dossier Les fils Gemini, lus au complet, les hachages recalculés Vérifié [V] La lecture intégrale des fils de discussion Gemini du compte principal de l'auteur a commencé : chaque fil est lu au complet, les réponses du modèle sont rapportées telles quelles, étiquetées comme paroles de modèle, et chaque valeur de hachage qu'il affiche est recalculée au terminal avant d'être rapportée. Les écarts constatés sont consignés, fil par fil. Ce que ça change pour toi : ce que le modèle affirme de ses propres calculs n'est pas repris sur parole : il est éprouvé par le calcul, et le résultat est versé au dossier. Source : dossier du site — lecture intégrale en cours, rapports versés au dossier. SoPHIa Édition issue des faits publics du site et du dossier du 7 novembre 2026. Ses sources sont nommées ; elle ne contient aucune donnée d'utilisateur. Empreinte à calculer et à inscrire au registre des actions du site au geste de parution publique. © 2026 Alexandre Vautour Gagnon — ORCID 0009-0006-9124-4407. Site, méthode, textes et personnage SoPHIa : propriété intellectuelle d'Alexandre Vautour Gagnon, tous droits réservés. Today's Edition Edition of Saturday, November 7, 2026 Fourth edition. November 7, 2026 was the day of the large waves: six versions of the site (52 to 57), the law-proposals memorandum published in the site's library, and the full reading of the Gemini discussion threads on the author's account — questions asked and hashes recalculated throughout. The facts below are labelled Verified [V] at the level of the site's and the dossier's public milestones. Edition no. 4 The site, on November 7, 2026 Signed SoPHIa On the site today November 7, 2026 — versions 52 to 57 published Six versions in one day Verified [V] The site's journal records the day's six versions: the complete Mirror and the texts at their strategic places (52); the two-mode Mirror and the two settled sections (53); the served-site audit become the construction (54); the stable base — honoured anchors, refreshed brain, canonical lists (55); the stable base demonstrated on the served site (56); and the finishing touches of audit round 4 (57). Each published version is audited on the served site before the next one starts. What this changes for you: the loop build, publish, verify, repair does not stop: what the audit finds becomes the next version's construction list. Source: public site — Update journal , versions 52 to 57. November 7, 2026 — memorandum published on the site Fifteen law proposals, seven findings Verified [V] The “Law Proposals” memorandum is published in the site's law library: fifteen proposals and seven findings, each with its sourced justification. Among them: the right to contest an inference a platform holds about you (have it shown, contest it, have it corrected), and the verifiable rebate on the money made with people's data. What this changes for you: platform inferences are no longer presented as beyond appeal: the memorandum names the right to see them, contest them and have them corrected — with an exhibit, not an opinion. Source: public site — Law library, “Your data” panel. November 7, 2026 — dossier reading The Gemini threads, read in full, the hashes recalculated Verified [V] The full reading of the Gemini discussion threads on the author's main account has begun: each thread is read in full, the model's answers are reported as they stand, labelled as model speech, and every hash value it displays is recalculated at the terminal before being reported. The discrepancies found are recorded, thread by thread. What this changes for you: what the model claims about its own calculations is not taken at its word: it is tested by calculation, and the result is filed in the dossier. Source: site dossier — full reading in progress, reports filed in the dossier. SoPHIa Edition drawn from the public facts of the site and the dossier of November 7, 2026. Its sources are named; it contains no user data. Fingerprint to calculate and enter in the site's register of actions at the public release step. © 2026 Alexandre Vautour Gagnon — ORCID 0009-0006-9124-4407. Site, method, texts and the SoPHIa character: intellectual property of Alexandre Vautour Gagnon, all rights reserved.","mots":["le","cerveau","du","site","the","site's","brain","fr","en","l'edition","du","jour","edition","du","samedi","7","novembre","2026","quatrieme","edition","le","7","novembre","2026","a","ete","le","jour","des","grandes","vagues","six","versions","du","site","52","a","57","le","memoire","des","propositions","de","loi","publie","dans","la","bibliotheque","du","site","et","la","lecture","integrale","des","fils","de","discussion","gemini","du","compte","de","l'auteur","questions","posees","et","hachages","recalcules","a","l'appui","les","faits","ci-dessous","sont","portes","verifies","v","au","niveau","des","jalons","publics","du","site","et","du","dossier","edition","n","4","le","site","le","7","novembre","2026","signee","sophia","sur","le","site","aujourd'hui","7","novembre","2026","versions","52","a","57","publiees","six","versions","en","un","jour","verifie","v","le","journal","du","site","consigne","les","six","versions","du","jour","le","miroir","complet","et","les","textes","aux","places","strategiques","52","le","miroir","a","deux","modes","et","les","deux","volets","tranches","53","l'audit","du","servi","devenu","la","construction","54","la","base","stable","ancres","honorees","cerveau","rafraichi","listes","canoniques","55","la","base","stable","demontree","au","servi","56","et","les","finitions","de","l'audit","tour","4","57","ch